2. **Prototype Chain Targeting**: When the unpatched `setter()` function processes index `1`, it evaluates `obj["__proto__"]`. In JavaScript, accessing a non-enumerable property like `__proto__` on any object resolves to its prototype (`Object.prototype`). By writing to this path, the library directly mutates `Object.prototype` instead of the input object.
