   The unhandled exception propagates to the top level, terminating the process. In production environments without these debug flags, this would manifest as a **CPU starvation attack**: malicious input consumes exponentially more cycles processing the regex, effectively hanging legitimate requests or crashing processes via out-of-memory / watchdog timeouts.

