```bash
node --regexp-backtracks-before-fallback=30000 exploit.js
```
On vulnerable versions of `ws` (pre-7.0.1 / commit fixing SNYK-JS-WS-1296835), you will observe the CPU spike followed by a terminating `RegExpError`. In patched versions, the code either throws a `RangeError` due to length sanitization early in handshake, or completes instantly due to regex optimization. This PoC safely isolates and proves the underlying parsing flaw.
